														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2740134">
									

<p>Remember in (bourgeois) economics class where they highlighted how a firm only hires new workers if their marginal utility outweighs the cost of their labor? While each new worker DOES contribute, past a certain point each contributes less and less, so a firm will only hire so many workers.</p>
<p>The same principle applies here. It's not that this will NEVER help anyone, it's just plain not worth adding to the pile. It's an even bigger waste when you consider, as I mentioned above, that this essay is unlikely to find its way into the hands of many who would read and get something useful out of it that they wouldn't out of existing guides.</p>
<p>Like Greenwolf said, users would likely be better served by increasing the information density in existing guides and removing redundant material. Aren't you a mod? You could actually make that happen.</p>

